-- status  : Open
-- author  : @mikedeng1
-- created : 2026-09-19T20:51:40.479497+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/2ca89b16-86bc-430d-93db-97417d322366
-- title:
--   Theorem 12.4 (Main) — online boosting regret bound (goal)
-- statement:
--   **Statement (Theorem 12.4, "Main," p. 200, PDF p. 222).** The predictions $x_t$ generated
--   by Algorithm 36 with $\delta = \sqrt{D^2/(\gamma N)}$, $\eta_i = \min\{2/i,1\}$ satisfy
--   $$\sum_{t=1}^T f_t(x_t) - \min_{h^\star\in CH(H)}\sum_{t=1}^T f_t(h^\star(a_t)) \le
--   \frac{5dGDT}{\gamma\sqrt N} + \frac{2GD}\gamma\mathrm{Regret}_T(W).$$
--
--   This is the chapter's payoff: given only black-box `γ`-WOCL access (no dependence on
--   $|H|$), Algorithm 36 achieves low regret against the **convex hull** of $H$ — a strictly
--   stronger comparator than the best single hypothesis in $H$, and meaningful even at $\gamma=1$
--   (a "weak" learner that already matches the best hypothesis in $H$, where the boosting
--   algorithm's payoff is purely the upgrade from $H$ to $CH(H)$).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $CH(H) = \mathrm{convexHull}\,\mathbb R\,H$ (Mathlib's own convex
--   hull, applied to $H$ viewed as a subset of the function space $A \to
--   \mathrm{EuclideanSpace}\,\mathbb R\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,n)$) — the book's own $\{\sum_{h\in
--   H}p_hh \mid p\in\Delta_H\}$, matched exactly by Mathlib's general convex-hull operation
--   rather than a finite-support-only reimplementation, since $H$ may be infinite. `Regret_T(W)`
--   is the weak learner's own regret bound, supplied via `hWOCL` (one `γ`-WOCL guarantee per
--   stage `i∈[1,N]`) as an explicit hypothesis of the theorem, not part of its conclusion — the
--   pitfall `BRIEF.md` flags most prominently. The running-time independence from `|H|`
--   mentioned in the surrounding prose is not part of this numbered theorem's mathematical
--   content and is not formalized.
--
--   A moderator change request (2026-09-19) caught two hypothesis-scope gaps: `hfG` originally
--   bounded each `f t`'s gradient only over `K`, but Lemma 12.3's proof (this mission's
--   `extension_approximation_and_monotonicity`) needs the bound at Algorithm 36's un-projected,
--   `1/γ`-scaled stage iterates, which generally leave `K` (p. 198's own standing assumption
--   that loss functions are defined, and gradient-bounded, over all of `R^d`) — `hfG` now bounds
--   the gradient everywhere, matching `extension_approximation_and_monotonicity`'s own
--   unrestricted hypothesis. `IsGammaWOCL` gained the `K`-parametrized range-bound precondition
--   described in its own `natural_language_statement`; `hWOCL`'s type is unchanged in shape
--   (`IsGammaWOCL K γ T a H (fun t => W t i) (fun t => fstage t i) RegretBoundW`, now with `K`
--   threaded through) and is still assumed as a hypothesis of the whole implication, matching
--   how the book's own proof does not re-derive the range bound at the point of use either.
-- source:
--   Hazan, Introduction to Online Convex Optimization, 2nd ed., arXiv:1909.05207v3, p. 200, Theorem 12.4 (PDF p. 222)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_OnlineConvexOpt_OnlineBoosting_Algorithm
import Definitions.Def_OnlineConvexOpt_OnlineBoosting_WOCL

namespace OnlineConvexOpt.OnlineBoosting

/-- Theorem 12.4, "Main" (Hazan, *Introduction to Online Convex Optimization*, 2nd ed.,
arXiv:1909.05207v3, p. 200, PDF p. 222). The predictions `x_t` generated by Algorithm 36 with
`δ = √(D²/(γN))`, `η_i = min{2/i,1}` satisfy
`∑_{t=1}^T f_t(x_t) - min_{h⋆∈CH(H)}∑_{t=1}^T f_t(h⋆(a_t)) ≤ (5dGDT)/(γ√N) + (2GD/γ)Regret_T(W)`.

`CH(H)` (the convex hull of the hypothesis class `H`) is `convexHull ℝ H`, viewing `H` as a set
in the function space `A → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)`. `RegretBoundW` is the weak learner's own
regret bound, a hypothesis of the theorem (via `hWOCL`, one `γ`-WOCL guarantee per stage
`i ∈ [1,N]`), not the boosting algorithm's own regret, which is exactly the conclusion. `hfG`
bounds the gradient of every `f t` over all of `E`, not just over `K`: the chapter's own standing
assumption (p. 198/PDF 220, "we assume that the loss functions `f ∈ F` are defined over all of
`R^d` to enable valid decisions outside of `K`") is needed because Algorithm 36's un-projected,
`1/γ`-scaled stage iterates `x^{i-1}_t` generally leave `K`, and Lemma 12.3's proof bounds `f t`'s
gradient there. -/
theorem online_boosting_regret
    {n : ℕ} (d : ℕ) (hd : d = n)
    (K : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (hKconv : Convex ℝ K) (hKne : K.Nonempty)
    (D G : ℝ) (hDpos : 0 < D) (hGpos : 0 < G) (hD : ∀ x ∈ K, ∀ y ∈ K, dist x y ≤ D)
    (γ : ℝ) (hγpos : 0 < γ) (hγ1 : γ ≤ 1)
    (N T : ℕ) (hN : 0 < N) (hT : 0 < T)
    (δ : ℝ) (hδ : δ = Real.sqrt (D ^ 2 / (γ * N)))
    (η : ℕ → ℝ) (hη : ∀ i : ℕ, 1 ≤ i → η i = min (2 / (i : ℝ)) 1)
    (A : Type*) (a : ℕ → A) (H : Set (A → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (f : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (hfconv : ∀ t, ConvexOn ℝ K (f t))
    (hfG : ∀ t, ∀ x, ∀ v, HasGradientAt (f t) v x → ‖v‖ ≤ G)
    (W x : ℕ → ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (fstage : ℕ → ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ)
    (xplay : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (hrun : IsOnlineBoostingRun K γ δ G N T η a f W x fstage xplay)
    (RegretBoundW : ℝ)
    (hWOCL : ∀ i : ℕ, 1 ≤ i → i ≤ N →
      IsGammaWOCL K γ T a H (fun t => W t i) (fun t => fstage t i) RegretBoundW)
    (hstar : A → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hstar_mem : hstar ∈ convexHull ℝ H)
    (hstar_min : ∀ h ∈ convexHull ℝ H,
      (∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (hstar (a t))) ≤ ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (h (a t))) :
    (∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (xplay t)) - ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (hstar (a t)) ≤
      (5 * d * G * D * T) / (γ * Real.sqrt N) + (2 * G * D / γ) * RegretBoundW := by sorry

end OnlineConvexOpt.OnlineBoosting
